# SRG-APP-000219-WSR-000190  -  CAT II
# The web server must restrict a consistent inbound source IP for the entire
# management session.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000219-WSR-000190
group:           V-264360
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001184
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise has no setting that binds an authenticated management
                 session to the source IP address it was established from. What the product
                 can do is restrict the set of addresses from which management connections
                 are accepted at all, through the source address list on the splunkd
                 management listener, and restrict general remote login. The criterion
                 tests only that share.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom non_empty
check:           server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom not_equals *
check:           server.conf [general] allowRemoteLogin not_equals always
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [general] allowRemoteLogin https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Binding a management session to the source IP address it was established
                 from - Splunk Enterprise exposes no per-session source address setting;
                 this is carried by a reverse proxy, load balancer or firewall placed in
                 front of the management port
external:        The permitted management source addresses themselves -
                 organization-defined network allowlist

citation:        server.conf.spec:1291 ([httpServer]) with :1345-1360 (acceptFrom =
                 <network_acl>, default "*" accept from anywhere); server.conf.spec:106-120
                 (allowRemoteLogin = always|never|requireSetPassword, "Controls remote
                 management by restricting general login", default requireSetPassword)
finding:         The splunkd management listener accepts connections from any source
                 address, or general remote login is set to always, so the application does
                 not restrict the inbound source of a management session to the extent the
                 product allows.
